posts.body:
@Tai_MT
I like a lot of the things you mention about your game! I especially like your Inn concept.
And I have a general idea of how to approach most of what I have on the list so far. I am just one of those people who has to implement it to make sure what I'm thinking will work actually works. That is one of the ways I learn, through experimentation. Especially with learning to use RPG Maker. I find that my ideas for implementation of something often have to be tweaked due to my lack of experience or knowledge or things I didn't fully conceptualize.
The random part of the choices matter aspect would be more about what choices a player might be offered and how NPCs react to the player based on things like reputation, charisma, skills checks, or even world biases. I would have to think seriously about how randomness might be worth putting into the results of choices in other aspects.
@Banana_Duck
I will be pursuing D&D style game play so dice rolls will definitely come into play for different results. But that only relates to combat and skill checks. I also want different experiences with exploration and adventuring, which is a huge part of many games.
